sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch04-01> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-01--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-01--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch04-01: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.29" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.288"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "not-empirically-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/none" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Wolfram's point is that when calculus and similar methods finish the job, the behavior they find is simple, and that textbooks are chosen for that amenability. That connection is built into what those methods can express. A survey of solved textbook systems would reproduce the selection rather than test a further empirical claim about number-based systems." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: The claim ties 'complete analysis by traditional mathematics' to 'fairly simple behavior' and explains textbook examples by that selection. Systems that traditional methods can solve are simple in the sense of those methods, so the outcome does not separate a factual regularity from the definition of analyzability." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The claim is close to a selection effect: textbooks keep systems that traditional analysis can finish, and those systems are then called simple.", "There is no independent catalog of 'all number-based systems traditional mathematics can analyze completely' whose behavior could come out complex." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-01--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch04-01 by Grok 4.7: 0.35" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.35"^^xsd:double ;
